  "Question": "What is the value of \\[ \\begin{aligned} &4 \\cdot (-1 + 2 - 3 + 4 - 5 + 6 \\\\ &\\qquad {}- 7 + \\cdots + 1000)? \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-10\\)",
    "B": "\\(0\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(500\\)",
    "E": "\\(2000\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Inside the parentheses, each negative odd number is followed by a positive even number that is one greater. Group these neighbors together:\n\\[\n(-1+2)+(-3+4)+\\cdots+(-999+1000).\n\\]\nEvery pair has sum \\(1\\). All \\(1000\\) terms are included exactly once, making \\(1000\\div2=500\\) pairs. Thus the value of the original expression is\n\\[\n4\\cdot500=2000.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(2000\\), choice E.",
